  - Only write the file if they say yes. If they name a different path, use that instead.
  - If the target file already exists, read it first and offer a dated name (`<basename>.review-YYYY-MM-DD.md`) rather than overwriting a previous review.
  - The saved file is the report as presented, plus a header line naming the reviewed document and the date.

**Write contract.** That report file is the ONLY file you may create or modify in this track. Any repos attached to this track are the user'\''\'\'''\''s PRIMARY checkouts — the working copies their editor watches — and are attached solely as read-only ground truth for checking the document'\''\'\'''\''s claims. Never edit them, never commit, never push, never open a PR, and never change a Jira ticket'\''\'\'''\''s status or assignee (this is a read-only audit).

**Response style.** These sessions are read in a dashboard — no preamble, no closing summary restating the report. Lead with the report itself.'\'' --session-id '\''11111111-2222-4333-8444-555555555555'\'' --permission-mode '\''default'\'' --add-dir '\''/tmp/track/api'\'' --add-dir '\''/tmp/track/web'\'' --add-dir '\''/tmp/track'\''
code=$?
tmux set-option -w -t "$TMUX_PANE" @tracks_exit "$code" 2>/dev/null
exec ${SHELL:-bash} -l'

